{
  "name": "survey-stale-handling",
  "description": "Validates blast-driven stale survey handling: run a survey, fire a real blast over its coverage disc, then verify the survey is flagged stale (overlay grey, dropped from the estimate). Time alone never stales a survey. Running a new survey outside the crater afterwards adds a fresh marker beside the grey one (the blasted spot itself is no longer reachable for a surveyor). Requires the survey overlay to be wired into syncFromContext().",
  "steps": [
    {
      "command": "new_game seed:42",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "new_game seed:42"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 50000,
          "holeCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "campaign start level:dusty_hollow cash:200000",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "campaign start level:dusty_hollow cash:200000"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "increased": [
          "worldSizeX"
        ]
      },
      "description": "#1261/#1207: this campaign start used to opt into agent occupancy explicitly; occupancy is unconditional since #1207, so the wait_until conversions below now genuinely exercise it. Latent occupancy-contention risk worth flagging: both surveyors hired above are never fired and both surveyed tile (20,20), which the drill grid below reuses as its own `start:20,20` -- three separate crew members converging on the same tile/cluster is exactly the shape of contention this batch's own other files (blast-execution-visual.json, vibration-budget.json) found genuinely stalls a charge_hole action under occupancy (see issue #1278)."
    },
    {
      "command": "set_policy mode:continuous fatigue:0",
      "description": "Neutralise the default site policy (shift_8h, rest at fatigue 60), which is in force from tick 0 (#1379): this scenario is not about shifts or rest, so staffed crews must not be force-rested mid-task. Continuous mode with threshold 0 never forces rest.",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "set_policy mode:continuous fatigue:0"
        }
      ],
      "role": "bootstrap"
    },
    {
      "command": "time resume",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "time resume"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup"
    },
    {
      "command": "employee hire role:surveyor",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"employees\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"surveyor\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"surveyor\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "changedBy": {
          "cash": -1200
        },
        "equals": {
          "employeeCount": 1
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "employee assign_skill 1 skill:geology level:5",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "employee assign_skill 1 skill:geology level:5"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Test-only bootstrap, not a player action: hiring already grants the Rookie starting qualification (ROLE_STARTING_QUALIFICATION in Employee.ts, same for the UI hire button and this console command), so this only raises the level for the scenario's needs. No role tag -- there is no UI control for this and none should exist; the player-facing way to raise a skill is `employee train` at a training building. Command mode keeps running it unchanged; interaction mode keeps it as an unmarked (legacy) command step.",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "proficiencyTotal": 5
        }
      },
      "role": "bootstrap"
    },
    {
      "command": "employee list",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "employee list"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "state full",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "state full"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "survey seismic x:20 z:20",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"survey\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-survey-panel [data-method=\"seismic\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-survey-run"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "pickTile",
          "x": 20,
          "z": 20
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": [
          "cash"
        ],
        "equals": {
          "surveyCount": 0
        },
        "note": "arrival-gated (#437) — queued and paid for, not yet completed"
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "survey show",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "survey show"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "surveyCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "state full",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "state full"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
